### Phasor Noise `cop/phasornoise` (11 October 2026)

- Summary: Generates phasor noise, which resembles a wave pattern. (11 October 2026)
- Overview: This node generates various noises defined by phasor kernels. A phasor kernel is a local filter that defines sine and cosine waves in a small neighborhood around a center point. By default, the noise resembles a wave pattern. When the Signature is any channel except Mono, the node generates additional phasor noises for each component of the set channel and (11 October 2026)
- Inputs: pos (An optional UV layer with a value that's used instead of the pixel's image ...); time (An optional layer with a value that each pixel uses for the time.); bias (An optional layer with a value that's used for the peak position of each ...); scale (An optional layer with a value that's multiplied by the Element Size.); direction (An optional UV layer to set the initial angle of phasor kernels.) (11 October 2026)
- Outputs: noise (The computed noise.) (11 October 2026)
- Parm Signature (signature; String; default default): The layer type that the source outputs. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Type Info (typeinfo; Menu; default 0): The type information for the resulting layer. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Rotate Channel (rotatechannel): When Signature is any channel except Mono, this is the amount to rotate the noise in the additional channels. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Range > Amplitude (amp; Float; default 0.5) [NOTE]: The amount by which to multiply the noise, which the node applies before the Center adjustment. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Range > Center (center; Float; default 0.5): The center of the output noise range, which offsets the pixel values. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Range > Noise Contrast (noisecontrast; Float; default 0): The amount of contrast to apply to the noise before the Amplitude and Center parameters. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Pattern > Type (type; Menu; default 0) [Phasor Wave | Phasor Noise | Gabor Noise | Intensity Field | Sine | Rectangle | Saw]: Sets the type of noise and, when set to Phasor Wave, the periodic function (wave type). (11 October 2026)
- Parm Pattern > Element Size (element; Float; default 0.5) [WARNING]: The size of the wave's width in the noise. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Pattern > Element Scale (elementscalex, elementscaley): When the Smallicon:BUTTONS/decompose_transforms Per-Component Controls button is on, this is the per-axis scaling of the element size. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Pattern > Offset (offsetx, offsety): The amount to offset the entire noise function in image coordinates. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Pattern > Tile Size (tilesizex, tilesizey) [NOTE]: The size of a single tile of noise. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Pattern > Wave Bias (wavebias; Float; default 0): When Type is Phasor Wave, this is the peak position of each periodic function. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Pattern > Blending Radius (blend; Float; default 1): The radius of the phasor kernels. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Pattern > Seed (seed; Int; default 0): The seed that the random number generator uses. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Pattern > Kernels (kernels; Int; default 6): The number of disk-shaped local regions where the primary sine and cosine waves are defined. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Bias > Blur (biasblur; Float; default 0.01): The amount to blur the input image. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Bias > Strength (biasstr; Float; default 0.5): The strength of bias blending. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Scale > Blur (scaleblur; Float; default 0.03): The amount to blur the input image. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Scale > Strength (scalestr; Float; default 0.3): The strength of scale blending. (11 October 2026)
- Parm 3D Noise > 3D Noise (use3d; Toggle; default False): Evaluates the noise in a 3D space. (11 October 2026)
- Parm 3D Noise > Animate (animate; Toggle; default False): Implicitly adds time to the third coordinate. (11 October 2026)
- Parm 3D Noise > Pulse Length (pulselength; Float; default 1): The interval length (in seconds) of the noise's pulse in the third dimension. (11 October 2026)
- Parm 3D Noise > Time Offset (timeoffset; Float; default 0): The amount of time (in seconds) that's added to the start frame. (11 October 2026)
- Parm 3D Noise > Time Scale (timescale; Float; default 1): The amount of time (in seconds) by which to multiply the start frame. (11 October 2026)
- Parm 3D Noise > Loop Length (sec) (looplength; Float; default 10): This is the time (in seconds) at which to repeat the noise. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Rotate > Rotate Pattern (firstrotatepattern; Float; default 0) [NOTE]: The amount to rotate the phasor kernels. (11 October 2026)
